{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05XJ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f : \\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$1$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0007": "$h : \\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{U}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{Y} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{U}\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$1$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{Y} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0013": "$$\n\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{U} =\n(\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{U})\n\\times_{(\\mathcal{Y} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{U})}\n\\mathcal{U}.\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-properties-lemma-etale-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c66ff3a78f8462c637934f69924883c699475f3d2e4d60feccd611db23574816", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:86732bd5f77d392e5a3f7a45492debe33311052a6cb35aa7e3e6e5c63d5073f1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a representable category fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a <MATH_0004>-morphism. We have to show that\n<MATH_0005> is representable by an\nalgebraic space and <ACCENT_0001>tale over <MATH_0006>.\nConsider the composition <MATH_0007>. Then\n<MATH_0008>\nis a <MATH_0009>-morphism between categories fibres in groupoids which are both\nrepresentable by algebraic spaces and both <ACCENT_0002>tale over <MATH_0010>.\nHence by\nProperties of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthis is represented by an <ACCENT_0003>tale morphism of algebraic spaces.\nFinally, we obtain the result we want as the morphism <MATH_0011> induces\na morphism <MATH_0012>\nand we have\n<MATH_0013>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6a29a75caf6251626545af64de3b855f2cd8a9beaa4e7e18b8d41ae2c17b15ed", "unit_id": "tag:05XK:proof"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05XJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}, \\mathcal{Y}, \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$1$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0008": "$Y$", "MATH_0009": "$Z$", "MATH_0010": "$S$", "MATH_0011": "$Y \\to Z$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{Y} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-stack-in-setoids-descent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d19ca4b7826c55d15cc1db37fa48bf87474962de29d6a6c81a3930e9542e741d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e95fa48365f2c3257161ee24c4fac1e9ce14481df1c6edd0ec09fc8e0c47b8bb", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be stacks in groupoids\nover <MATH_0002>. Suppose that <MATH_0003>\nand <MATH_0004> are <MATH_0005>-morphisms.\nIf\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0006>, <MATH_0007> are representable by algebraic spaces\n<MATH_0008>, <MATH_0009> over <MATH_0010>,\n<STRUCT_0003> the associated morphism of algebraic spaces <MATH_0011> is surjective,\nflat and locally of finite presentation, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0012> is a stack in\nsetoids,\n<STRUCT_0005>\nthen <MATH_0013> is a stack in setoids.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dd3c5f60a9c636da8dc1f35ab4756bf4816519ec077c37001fdcb8549e2613cd", "unit_id": "tag:05XL:statement"}
